          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_11 Remark
            %p
              This is essentially the short exact sequence whose form is familiar from the traditional definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
              only up to the following slight nuances in notation:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  The cohomology groups of the short exact sequence above denote the groups obtained in the given
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mo =
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9ELieGrpd"} ∞LieGrpd
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = U(1) =\mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |X| \in Top
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                  of a paracompact manifold
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n(X,\mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z})
                  above is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi H
                            %mi sing
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi Π
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{n+1}_{sing}({|\Pi X|},\mathbb{Z})
              %li
                %p
                  The fact that on the left of the short exact sequence for differential cohomology we have the de Rham cohomology set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi H
                          %mi dR
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{dR}^n(X,A)
                  instead of something like the set of all flat forms as familiar from
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
              is because the latter has no
            %p
              intrinsic meaning but depends on a choice of model. After fixing a specific
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              we can consider instead of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi dR
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi dR
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{dR}^{n+1}(X,A) \to \mathbf{H}_{dR}(X, \mathbf{B}^{n+1}A)
              the inclusion of the set of objects
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi cl
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                      %mi ℝ
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℝ
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Omega_{cl}^{n+1}(X,A) {:=} \mathbb{R}Hom_C(X, \mathbf{B}^{n+1}A )_0
                      \\hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}Hom_C(X, \mathbf{B}^{n+1}A )
              %a{:href => "#DiffCohIsWellDefined"} above observation
              this only adds multiple copies of the homotopy types of the connected components of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mi diff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi n
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{diff}(X, \mathbf{B}^n A)
            %p
              For a detailed discussion of the relation to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
              see at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
              the section
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/smooth infinity-groupoid#DiffCohomologyAbstractProperties"} Abstract properties of differential cohomology
          %p
            In view of the second of these points one can make a
            %em choice
            of cover in order to present the twisting cocycles functorially. To that end, let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^{n+1}_{cl}(-,A) \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^{n+1}A
          %p
            denote a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism
            out of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated"} 0-truncated
            object which we suggestively denote by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{n+1}_{cl}(-,A)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_29 Definition
            %p
              With a choice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{n+1}_{cl}(-,A) \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^{n+1}A
              fixed, we say an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
              is
              %strong
                dR-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
              if the induced morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{H}(X, \Omega^{n+1}_{cl}(-,A))
                    \\to
                    \\mathbf{H}(X, \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^{n+1}A)
            %p
              is itself an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism
              (of
              = succeed ")s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_12 Remark
            %p
              A morphism of
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category#EffectiveEpisOfInfinityGroupoids"} here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{n+1}_{cl}(-,A)
              is assumed to be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated"} 0-truncated
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^{n+1}_{cl}(X,A) := \mathbf{H}(X, \Omega^{n+1}_{cl}(-,A))
            %p
              is 0-truncated. Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is dR-projective precisely if the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{n+1}_{cl}(X,A)
              contains representatives of all intrinsic de Rham cohomology classes of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              In terms of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercohomology"} hypercohomology
              this may be thought of as saying that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is dR-projective if every de Rham hypercohomology class on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has a representative by a globally defined differential form. In models of cohesion we typically have that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
              are dR-projective, but nontrivial
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_30 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n A_{conn}
              for the
              = succeed "-pullback" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
